# id: M64-secondary-commits-at-its-own-timestamp
# covering-test: TestTransactionAtomicityOracleReportsNothing
# package: ./sim/hunt/
# expect: killed
# power-seeds: 300
# power-floor: 1
# power-ceiling: 30
# power-measured: PENDING
# mutates: a transaction's secondaries commit one logical tick after its primary. Each key's own history is perfectly ordinary -- one prewrite, one commit, ascending timestamps -- so nothing that looks at a single key can see it, and every replica agrees. A reader between the two timestamps sees half the transaction, which is the definition of atomicity broken
